---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<Page
	title="Open a shared album · TagTape"
	description="Someone shared a TagTape album with you: its details and track links, to make on your own computer."
	scripts
	noindex
>
	<!-- Shown until the script has found an album in the address (and when
	     there is none, or scripts are off). -->
	<section id="share-intro" class="max-w-2xl py-8 lg:py-14">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Shared albums</h1>
		<p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
			In TagTape, <span class="font-medium text-foreground">Share</span> on an album gives a small file or a link.
			It holds the album's details, the track titles and the track links: what someone typed, never the music.
			Whoever opens it makes the album on their own computer, over their own connection.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
			A share link carries the album inside the link itself, after the <code>#</code>. That part of an address is
			never sent to a website, so nothing is uploaded to TagTape or anyone else, and there is no list of shared
			albums anywhere.
		</p>
		<noscript>
			<p class="mt-6 border bg-card p-4 text-sm">
				This page needs JavaScript to read the album out of the link. Without it, open TagTape and use
				<span class="font-medium">File &gt; Open Album File</span> with a shared <code>.tagtape</code> file instead.
			</p>
		</noscript>
		<p class="mt-6">
			<a href={`${base}/#download`} class="border bg-card px-4 py-2.5 font-medium hover:bg-muted">Get TagTape</a>
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="share-problem" hidden class="max-w-2xl py-8 lg:py-14">
		<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">This link can't be opened</h1>
		<p id="share-problem-text" class="mt-4 border bg-card p-4"></p>
		<p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
			The link may have been cut short on the way. Ask for it again, or for the album as a
			<code>.tagtape</code> file.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="share-album" hidden class="py-8 lg:py-14">
		<p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-muted-foreground uppercase">An album shared with you</p>
		<h1 id="share-title" class="mt-1 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight break-words sm:text-4xl"></h1>
		<p id="share-artist" class="mt-1 text-lg text-muted-foreground"></p>
		<p id="share-details" class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground"></p>

		<div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
			<a id="share-open" href={`${base}/#download`} class="bg-primary px-5 py-3 font-medium text-primary-foreground hover:opacity-90"
				>Open in TagTape</a
			>
			<a id="share-save" href={`${base}/#download`} class="border bg-card px-5 py-3 font-medium hover:bg-muted"
				>Save as a .tagtape file</a
			>
		</div>
		<p id="share-too-long" hidden class="mt-3 max-w-2xl border bg-card p-3 text-sm">
			This album is too large to open with one click. Save it as a file, then open the file with TagTape
			(<span class="font-medium">File &gt; Open Album File</span>, or double-click it).
		</p>
		<p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">
			Nothing happens until you press Make album in the app. No TagTape yet?{" "}
			<a href={`${base}/#download`} class="font-medium text-foreground underline underline-offset-4">Download it</a>,
			then come back to this page.
		</p>

		<h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Tracks</h2>
		<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
			Each track's link points at the site named beside it. Open the album only if you trust where it came from.
		</p>
		<ol id="share-tracks" class="mt-4 divide-y border bg-card"></ol>
	</section>

	<script src="../scripts/open.ts"></script>
</Page>
